# Logic equivalence check of repair_design's output, following the recipe
# OpenLane uses in scripts/yosys/logic_equiv_check.tcl.
#
# Four attempts before this one failed (see NOTES.md). A literature check on
# 2026-09-03 explained each:
#
#   1/2. `equiv_make` matches WIRE NAMES, not compare points. Comparing a
#        Yosys hierarchical netlist against an OpenROAD flat one puts almost
#        no names in common, which is why 55K cells yielded 86 equivalence
#        points with enormous proof cones. Both inputs here are written by
#        OpenROAD, so they share one name domain.
#   3.   A k-padded sequential miter under `sby prove` is k-induction over
#        the whole design. Buffer insertion and gate resizing are a
#        COMBINATIONAL problem once you cut at the flops, so that handed the
#        solver a far harder question than the one being asked.
#   4.   `formal_pdk_proc.py` was unnecessary: `read_liberty` WITHOUT `-lib`
#        builds real functional models from each cell's `function` attribute.
#
# Buffers are never compare points. Inserting 10,000 of them adds zero
# compare points and only lengthens combinational cones, which structural
# hashing collapses. The compare-point set is fixed by the flop and port
# set, and repair_design changes neither.
#
#   usage: yosys -s experiments/openroad_repair/lec_openlane.ys

read_liberty -ignore_miss_func -ignore_miss_dir /home/toshn/sta_work/sky130hd_tt.lib
read_verilog /home/toshn/or_repair/prerepair.v
splitnets -ports
hierarchy -top bench_top
flatten
rename -top gold
design -stash gold

read_liberty -ignore_miss_func -ignore_miss_dir /home/toshn/sta_work/sky130hd_tt.lib
read_verilog /home/toshn/or_repair/repaired.v
splitnets -ports
hierarchy -top bench_top
flatten
rename -top gate
design -stash gate

design -copy-from gold -as gold gold
design -copy-from gate -as gate gate

equiv_make gold gate equiv
prep -flatten -top equiv
equiv_status

# Every flop in this benchmark has an ASYNCHRONOUS active-low reset, by the
# RTL's own stated rule. Yosys' SAT backend has no model for an async FF and
# says so: "No SAT model available for async FF cell ($_DFF_PN0_). Consider
# running `async2sync` or `clk2fflogic` first." async2sync rewrites the async
# reset into synchronous logic; it is applied to the merged design, so gold
# and gate are transformed identically and the comparison stays sound.
# clk2fflogic is the heavier alternative and is what made the divider proof
# intractable in experiments/fsm_reencode/, so async2sync is the right one.
async2sync
equiv_status

# Cheap structural sweep first, then SAT, then induction only if needed.
equiv_struct
equiv_status
equiv_simple -seq 10
equiv_status
equiv_induct -seq 4
equiv_status -assert
